  "title": "Empathize with Others’ Pain",
  "description": "When someone shares their pain: - Pause judgments: Avoid assuming they’re exaggerating. - Reflect on your experience: Remember times when your pain felt real but others doubted it. - Listen fully: Focus on understanding rather than comparing. Example: A friend says they’re struggling with back pain. Instead of dismissing it, acknowledge their feelings: \"That sounds tough.\"",
